==Finnish==

===Etymology===
Possibly a [[Proto-Baltic]] loan. Cognates include Karelian {{m|krl|siibi}}, Ludian {{m|lud|siib}} and Estonian {{m|et|tiib}}.

===Noun===
{{head|fi|noun}}

# A [[wing]] (''animal appendage for flying'').
# A wing (''airplane part'').
# A wing (''part of building'').
# A wing (''fraction of political movement'').
# A wing (''slang: human hand'').
# A [[sail]] (''blade of a windmill'').
# A [[blade]] or a [[paddle]] of a water wheel or a paddlewheel.
# A blade of a turbine or a propeller.
# {{lb|fi|idiomatic}} A [[mood]].
#:* ''olla siipi maassa'' (lit. "to have a wing on the ground", as an injured bird may have)
#:** to be depressed

